LogicalDash@gmail.com wrote:

> I'm a Nethack n00b, trying out the Gnome version.

> The default 16x16 tiles are a bit small for my
> tastes; I want to enable the 32x32 ones that are
> available in Game -> Change Settings.  But every
> time I choose that option, the game quits on me.

> How can I get the 32x32 tiles to work?

You need to name the file by a sufficient relative /
absolute (maybe that will work) filepathname, and
specify the tile dimensions, in your NetHack
defaults file, before you start a game.

In MS-Windows that's file "defaults.nh"; if your
Gnome-containing OS is Linux, that's probably your
".nethackrc" file in your home directory, which you
may need to create from the system one.

An example of how that would look is here:

# Use the optional 32x32 (large) tiles
OPTIONS=tile_file:tiles32.bmp, tile_width:32, tile_height:32

This can be mind-destroying to get right, because of
problems among where NetHack thinks its local
directory is, where the 32x32 tileset is, how you
are allowed to spell the filepathname, how you have
to spell the defaults file name, where you have to
put that file, what permissions you need to get
correct, and just general software hostility to the
user, so if you don't have luck quickly, get help
from a local Gnome user. I think for at least one of
my three Linux implementations of NetHack, I never
was able to change to large tiles.

To say that the NetHack docs for each implementation
need to spell out in excruciating detail how to do
exactly what you are doing for that specific
implementation, is belaboring the obvious, but they
don't, so getting it right is a heaping double
helping of Not Much Fun.

